            <ArticleTitle>Intracavitary course of the right coronary artery: an increasingly recognized anomaly by coronary computed tomography angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>W77-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RTI.0b013e3181b71798</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary computed tomography angiography is being increasingly used for evaluation of coronary artery anatomy. We present a case report in which coronary computed tomography angiography detected an uncommon intracavitary course of the right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
